WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:38.635
Tonight the planet tells you what it does after dark.

2
00:01:08.640 --> 00:02:07.703
A seal asleep in a pocket of air, warm below zero.

3
00:02:37.700 --> 00:03:37.520
Under the ice, the sea is quieter than any room you know.

4
00:04:07.520 --> 00:05:07.158
The fennec has a heart that gains seventy beats in moonlight.

5
00:05:37.160 --> 00:06:05.181
Sand is sunlight, stored.

6
00:06:05.181 --> 00:06:37.686
The camels kneel to the moon.

7
00:07:07.690 --> 00:08:06.779
Sperm whales sleep hanging like upside-down ivy, still as chandelier lights.

8
00:08:36.780 --> 00:09:38.142
A whale song can cross one hundred kilometres of dark water.

9
00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:14.982
Fourth night.

10
00:10:14.982 --> 00:10:26.035
No instruments moved.

11
00:10:26.035 --> 00:10:36.561
The sea sang anyway.

12
00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.928
Far to the south of the ice, the night turns warm.

13
00:11:09.928 --> 00:11:13.768
In the Amazon rainforest, darkness has its own heartbeat.

14
00:11:13.768 --> 00:11:21.448
The canopy closes like a quilt, leaves pressing against leaves, and beneath it the world slows to a gentle murmur.

15
00:11:21.448 --> 00:11:30.813
Rain begins without warning — soft, patient, curtain-light — and the trees hold it, letting only the faintest drops reach the forest floor.

16
00:11:30.813 --> 00:11:33.440
Everything here is already half asleep.

17
00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:01.341
High in the branches, the sloth has not moved for hours.

18
00:12:01.341 --> 00:12:07.471
It sleeps beneath its own living shade, a small green garden growing quietly in its fur.

19
00:12:07.471 --> 00:12:13.880
Fireflies rise from the understory in slow constellations, blinking, fading, blinking again.

20
00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:20.706
Somewhere near the river, a small night-dweller takes one careful step and slips out of the light.

21
00:12:20.706 --> 00:12:23.423
The forest does not need to know where.

22
00:12:23.423 --> 00:12:24.468
It breathes in…

23
00:12:24.468 --> 00:12:25.652
and breathes out…

24
00:12:25.652 --> 00:12:27.324
and the rain keeps time.

25
00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:54.589
Higher still, the night becomes almost weightless.

26
00:12:54.589 --> 00:13:03.218
On the roof of the mountains, the snow holds the last light like porcelain, and the moon — nearly full — climbs the wall of the sky.

27
00:13:03.218 --> 00:13:05.244
Nothing moves on the ridge now.

28
00:13:05.244 --> 00:13:07.271
Even the wind has gone to rest.

29
00:13:07.271 --> 00:13:17.469
Down in the valley the contours soften, the rivers turn to silver threads of sound, and the shadow of the great peak stretches calmly across half the world.

30
00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:47.168
It was here, on nights like this, that we first learned to keep our thoughts quiet.

31
00:13:47.168 --> 00:13:55.956
A small observatory stands alone at the edge of the cold, its glass eye open, drinking starlight older than the mountain itself.

32
00:13:55.956 --> 00:13:56.848
We are small.

33
00:13:56.848 --> 00:14:01.105
The mountain has always known that, and it is gentle about it.

34
00:14:01.105 --> 00:14:03.645
Look up: the stars are not scattered.

35
00:14:03.645 --> 00:14:08.794
They are arranged — patiently — like furniture in a room designed for rest.

36
00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:38.480
And then, above the same ice where our seal is sleeping, the sky remembers itself.

37
00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:46.112
Green first — a breath of mint-light crossing the stars — then violet, then red, moving like silk under water.

38
00:14:46.112 --> 00:14:53.537
The aurora is the earth's lullaby to itself: the solar wind turning to light as it meets the breathing air.

39
00:14:53.537 --> 00:14:57.076
The bear lifts its head once, watches, and settles.

40
00:14:57.076 --> 00:14:58.672
Nobody keeps time here.

41
00:14:58.672 --> 00:15:02.557
The light moves, the ice answers quietly, and the world…

42
00:15:02.557 --> 00:15:03.876
goes back to sleep.

43
00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:49.093
Sleep like a seal under the ice.

44
00:15:49.093 --> 00:16:08.907
The earth is a warm room tonight.
